> Could someone clarify:
>
>  1. Do cfi.robust and rmsea.robust implement Savalei’s cML(D),s
>     corrections?

Yes. If they are available (i.e., not NA), these are the ones you should
report.

>  2. Is tli.robust based on the same correction?

Yes.

>  3. For binary WLSMV models, should the .robust values be reported in

>     preference to the .scaled values?

Yes. The .scaled values are only printed for two reasons: 1) often, when
the correlation matrix of poly/tetra-choric correlations is not positive
definite, we cannot compute the .robust versions, and the .scaled
versions are the fallback; 2) reproducibility: many older studies only
report the .scaled versions (because the .robust ones did not exist yet)

>  4. What do the unqualified values represent in this setting?

Not sure what you mean by this?

Yves.

--
Yves Rosseel
Department of Data Analysis, Ghent University

