On Sun, Aug 30, 2026 at 9:52 AM adri...@gmail.com <adri...@gmail.com> wrote:

> A structural model I fitted in lavaan 0.7-2 (WLSMV, ordered indicators) converged normally, issued no warnings, and returned TRUE for lavInspect(fit, "post.check"). The solution was nevertheless improper: psi had an eigenvalue of -0.269, because the freely estimated residual covariances among three single-indicator endogenous outcomes were far larger than their residual variances allow, giving residual correlations of -3.55 and -2.28.
>
> This is documented behaviour, not a bug. check.post <http://check.post> verifies the variances and the model-implied covariance matrices, and both of those were fine here: the smallest eigenvalues of cov.lv <http://cov.lv> and cov.ov were 0.285 and 0.133.
>
> Would it be worth extending check.post <http://check.post>, or adding a separate warning, to psi and theta? The impossible values are already visible in the Std.all column of summary(), but among sixty other numbers they are easy to read past when a model has otherwise converged cleanly.
